# Accepted dependency vulnerabilities (M6 Task 6.7). Every entry MUST have: reason, evidence, owner, expiry (exp:),
# and a risk-register / vulnerability-report reference. After the exp: date Trivy stops ignoring the entry, so the
# gate fails again until the issue is fixed or the acceptance is re-reviewed.
# Policy (docs/operations/devsecops-baseline.md#exceptions): a scanner-Critical CVE may be accepted ONLY when
#   (1) there is no open-source fix on the supported framework line, (2) the vendor rates it below High, and
#   (3) the vulnerable feature is verifiably not used. Otherwise it is fixed, not ignored.

# Spring Framework 6.2.x: open-source fix only in 7.0.9 (Spring Boot 4); 6.2.20 is enterprise-only.
# Vendor severity MEDIUM. Requires XsltView rendering behind a catch-all /** mapping. Not used: all controllers are
# @RestController (JSON only), no XsltView, no view resolvers or template engines (grep evidence in VULN-M6-019).
# Owner: Backend lead. Remove with the Spring Boot 4 migration (backlog B-18, risk R-17).
CVE-2026-47884 exp:2026-12-31

# Spring Framework 6.2.x: same fix situation as above. Vendor severity LOW. Requires Server-Sent Events carrying view
# fragments. Not used: no SseEmitter / ResponseBodyEmitter / text/event-stream anywhere (VULN-M6-019).
# Owner: Backend lead. Remove with B-18.
CVE-2026-47890 exp:2026-12-31
